==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|nephritick}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|neufretic}}, from {{der|en|ML.|nefreticus}}; compare {{w|Classical Latin}} {{m|la|nephrīticus}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|nephritis|-ic}} = {{confix|en|nephr|gloss1=kidney|itis|gloss2=inflammation|ic|gloss3=related}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, relating to, or affected with [[nephritis]] or {{w|nephritic syndrome}}.
#: {{cot|en|nephrotic}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Of or relating to the [[kidney]]s.<!--archaic because sense is not in current use by clinicians except [[catachresis|catachrestically]]-->
#: {{syn|en|nephric|renal}}

